"""Generated fetch-decode artifact-missing custody band 17.

Scenario slice 11520..12239 of 21600 lattice rows over (stage, reason, shape,
disposition switch, attempt, error class). Every cell drives the real custody
surface -- ``report_terminal_quarantine`` over a recording logger double,
``validation_disposition_failure`` under both switch values, the closed store
validators, the worker evidence mapper, the persist tail's verdicts and the
artifact-missing classifier -- and asserts one property against the
independent custody spec embedded below. The spec mirrors the documented
contract (the closed stage and reason vocabularies with the
``decode_artifact_missing`` join, the four terminal report arms in precedence
order with their exact lines, the evidence collapse to ``unknown``, the
stage-scoped disposition families, the type-only storage-404 verdict), never
the module under test. The emitter and its cross-verification formulations
live outside the tree. Do not edit frozen expectations by hand.

Rows are encoded as integers: ``_row(i)`` decodes stage ``i // 720 % 6``,
reason ``i // 40 % 18``, shape ``i // 10 % 4``, switch ``i // 5 % 2``,
attempt ``i % 5 + 1`` and error class ``i // 4320 % 5``. Each test pins one
(row, facet) cell of the lattice.

Failure-Class: FC-fetch-decode-artifact-notfound-walks-gpu-ladder-as-unclassified-worker-fault
"""

import pytest

pytestmark = [pytest.mark.filterwarnings('ignore::DeprecationWarning')]


